This crate is a clean Rust implementation of bcrypt (Provos & Mazières,
USENIX 1999) following the OpenBSD semantics that are the de-facto standard.

The vendored C reference implementation under `crypt_blowfish/` is Openwall
crypt_blowfish 1.3 by Solar Designer, which is placed in the public domain
("No copyright is claimed, and the software is hereby placed in the public
domain"). It is used only by this crate's tests and benchmarks as a
differential reference; it is not linked into the library.

The Blowfish P-array and S-box initial values in `src/consts.rs` are the
hexadecimal digits of the fractional part of pi, transcribed from that
public-domain source and cross-checked against OpenBSD `blowfish.c`.
